Why Is Demand Increasing
Industrial Automation: Manufacturers are integrating humanoid robots into assembly and production environments, increasing demand for precise joint torque feedback and force control.
Healthcare Robotics: Robotic exoskeletons and surgical-assistance systems require accurate torque sensing for controlled movement, assistance, and delicate force management.
AI-Enabled Control: Edge computing and AI-enhanced torque loops enable faster force processing and lower communication latency, supporting safer human-robot interaction.

Humanoid Robotics Watch: Precision Sensing Becomes Essential
Torque sensors are becoming a critical component of humanoid robot architectures because they provide real-time information about forces acting at joints such as shoulders, elbows, hips, knees, and wrists. Advances in miniaturization, multi-axis sensing, edge processing, and advanced materials are helping sensor manufacturers meet increasingly demanding robotics requirements.

